    topicKey: "disturbance",
    notes: "CO added - verified this session (statute walk + full-library audit; content itself unchanged WY added 2026-08-21 (full-library cross-check pass): generic mechanics, no CO-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with WY findings from this project. | NE extended (session 2, whole-library generic-clause audit): generic mechanics, no NE-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with NE findings from this project. | MN extended (Minnesota session, whole-library audit): generic mechanics, already vetted against KS/NE's prohibited-lease-provisions statutes (the strictest bar found in this project to date) since this clause was already tagged KS;NE; no MN-specific statutory language or number identified in this session's statute walk that conflicts. No exculpatory/liability-waiver language present. | ND ADDED 2026-09-06 (ND re-audit, exhaustive generic-clause audit prompted by the checklist-to-CSV reconciliation screen). ND's ORIGINAL whole-library audit was written up in its log but largely never executed against the CSV -- ND was shipped 'complete' with 18 displayable LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 61-75 for CO/WY/KS/NE/MN. This row is generic boilerplate carrying no ND-specific statutory interaction; ND's ch. 47-16 was read in full from primary text this session and no conflict was identified. LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK: North Dakota has NO enumerated prohibited-lease-provisions statute (confirmed this session -- § 47-16-02 is a maximum-term cap, and § 47-16-13.3 supplies only case-by-case unconscionability). The exculpation exposure that forced fixes to this clause family in KS and NE therefore does not arise for ND, same reasoning as the WY addendum. 5a.1 JUDGMENT: UNIFORM -- states field changed, clause TEXT unchanged, no re-review owed on existing tags. | SD ADDED 2026-09-07 (SD re-audit, Tier A of the L.2 exhaustive generic-clause audit). SD displayed only 13 LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 60-75 for every other state; 46 generics had no SD tag and no SD override. Triaged per L.2, not bulk-extended. Tier A = boilerplate with no SD statutory interaction, or self-limiting text that defers to applicable law. S5a.1 JUDGMENT: adding a state tag changes `states` only - no bodyText, rule_type or content_type change - so no other tagged state's rendering is affected and NO propagation to other state logs is owed. State-driven, not uniform. CA: extended to California 2026-09-19 after re-screen against the full CA pass (the extend manifest had deferred tagging until the blocked set was resolved, and the step was then missed). No CA conflict found. | NV: Read in full 2026-09-24 against NRS 118A (revisor text Rev. 4/15/2026, 2025 session incorporated). Applies as written; tracks 118A.310(1)(g). | TX: Read in full 2026-09-25 against Tex. Prop. Code ch. 92 (full chapter, section-open; Justia 2025 host copy with per-section history lines). Applies as written. No Texas interaction found in ch. 92. | NJ: added 2026-09-26 (tag-first screen, instruction 26). No NJ conflict. Disorderly conduct is an Anti-Eviction ground only after written notice to cease (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1(b)). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | FL: Applies as written (tag-first screen, instruction 26). Tracks Fla. Stat. §83.52(7). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | AZ: Applies as written. Mirrors A.R.S. §33-1341(7); §33-1368(F) makes the tenant responsible for guests' lease violations the tenant could reasonably foresee. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | ND 2026-09-28: the LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK above is withdrawn as to any clause disclaiming liability for the landlord's own violation of law. North Dakota does have enumerated bans outside its landlord-tenant title: N.D.C.C. §§9-08-02 (exculpation), 9-08-03 (penalties), 9-08-04 (liquidated damages) and 9-08-05 (restricting enforcement). See edu-prohibited-lease-terms-nd. | GA: Applies as written. Threats to the personal safety of the landlord, staff or another tenant, and intentional damage, are carved out of the retaliation defense (O.C.G.A. § 44-7-24(d)(2)(B)). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | NC: Applies as written. Tenant duties in N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-43(a) are consistent. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | SC: Tagged. Mirrors the tenant duty not to disturb other tenants' peaceful enjoyment (S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-510(7)). | TN: Tagged 2026-09-28 (section text read 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser (Justia host copy of the 2025 Tennessee Code with history lines; 2025-2026 public chapters screened; TN log §1)). Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-401(5) (Act counties): tenant must not disturb neighbors' peaceful enjoyment. TN-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. | VA: Tagged 2026-09-28. VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Read against the official Code of Virginia section-open (law.lis.virginia.gov; VA log §1). Basis: Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1227(A)(12): tenant responsible for own and consenting persons' conduct so neighbors' peaceful enjoyment is not disturbed. | AL: Tagged. Matches the tenant's statutory duty not to disturb neighbors' peaceful enjoyment and not to damage the premises (Ala. Code § 35-9A-301(6)-(7)). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | PA: Tagged. Mirrors the statutory tenant duty in 3+-household buildings (68 P.S. § 250.503-A(2), Act § 503-A). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | UT: Consistent with Utah Code Ann. § 57-22-5(2)(b) (no interference with another renter's peaceful enjoyment); the clause reaches further by contract. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IL: Tagged. No Illinois statute on tenant conduct clauses located. Read section-open 2026-09-30 (IL log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | ID: Lawful as written. Read section-open 2026-09-30 from legislature.idaho.gov (ID log s1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | MO: Applies as written. Consistent with Mo. Rev. Stat. § 441.630 (occupant duties) and the nuisance statutes (edu-nuisance-actions-mo). Read section-open 2026-09-30 (MO log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IN: Applies as written. A tenant who creates a drug nuisance may be ordered to vacate within 72 hours (Ind. Code § 32-30-8-11; edu-drug-nuisance-in). Read section-open 2026-09-30 from iga.in.gov (IN log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | OK: Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 127(6): the tenant shall not disturb, or allow persons, animals or pets to disturb, other tenants' quiet and peaceful enjoyment. Read section-open 2026-09-30 to 2026-10-01 from oklegislature.gov (OK log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | MI: Applies as written. Read section-open 2026-10-01 from legislature.mi.gov (MI log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IA: Applies as written; mirrors the tenant duty in Iowa Code § 562A.17(7).",
