    notes: "CO added - verified this session (statute walk + full-library audit; content itself unchanged WY added 2026-08-21 (full-library cross-check pass): generic mechanics, no CO-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with WY findings from this project. | NE extended (session 2, whole-library generic-clause audit): generic mechanics, no NE-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with NE findings from this project. | MN extended (Minnesota session, whole-library audit): generic mechanics compatible; MN's utility-disconnection prohibition (§ 504B.216, subd. 12, for shared-metered buildings) and unlawful-ouster provisions (§§ 504B.221, 504B.225, 504B.231) reinforce rather than conflict with this clause. | ND ADDED 2026-09-06 (ND re-audit, exhaustive generic-clause audit prompted by the checklist-to-CSV reconciliation screen). ND's ORIGINAL whole-library audit was written up in its log but largely never executed against the CSV -- ND was shipped 'complete' with 18 displayable LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 61-75 for CO/WY/KS/NE/MN. This row is generic boilerplate carrying no ND-specific statutory interaction; ND's ch. 47-16 was read in full from primary text this session and no conflict was identified. LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK: North Dakota has NO enumerated prohibited-lease-provisions statute (confirmed this session -- § 47-16-02 is a maximum-term cap, and § 47-16-13.3 supplies only case-by-case unconscionability). The exculpation exposure that forced fixes to this clause family in KS and NE therefore does not arise for ND, same reasoning as the WY addendum. 5a.1 JUDGMENT: UNIFORM -- states field changed, clause TEXT unchanged, no re-review owed on existing tags. | SD ADDED 2026-09-07 (SD re-audit, Tier A of the L.2 exhaustive generic-clause audit). SD displayed only 13 LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 60-75 for every other state; 46 generics had no SD tag and no SD override. Triaged per L.2, not bulk-extended. Tier A = boilerplate with no SD statutory interaction, or self-limiting text that defers to applicable law. S5a.1 JUDGMENT: adding a state tag changes `states` only - no bodyText, rule_type or content_type change - so no other tagged state's rendering is affected and NO propagation to other state logs is owed. State-driven, not uniform. CA: extended to California 2026-09-19 after re-screen against the full CA pass (the extend manifest had deferred tagging until the blocked set was resolved, and the step was then missed). No CA conflict found. | NV: Read in full 2026-09-24 against NRS 118A (revisor text Rev. 4/15/2026, 2025 session incorporated). Applies as written. | TX: Read in full 2026-09-25 against Tex. Prop. Code ch. 92 (full chapter, section-open; Justia 2025 host copy with per-section history lines). Applies as written. Tenant-side duty; no conflict with s92.008. | NJ: added 2026-09-26 (tag-first screen, instruction 26). No NJ conflict. Owner-side counterpart: N.J.A.C. 5:10-4.2 and N.J.S.A. 2C:33-11.1 (shut-off to regain possession is forcible entry and detainer). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | FL: Applies as written (tag-first screen, instruction 26). Tenant-side duty. The landlord-side shut-off ban is §83.67(1) (edu-prohibited-practices-fl). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | FL: Fla. Stat. §180.135(4) (read from Taylor's paste 2026-09-26): if a Part II tenant does not pay a city for utility, water or sewer service, the landlord may start eviction proceedings; edu-utility-former-occupant-fl. | AZ: Applies as written. No conflict with A.R.S. §§33-1341, 33-1364. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | ND 2026-09-28: the LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK above is withdrawn as to any clause disclaiming liability for the landlord's own violation of law. North Dakota does have enumerated bans outside its landlord-tenant title: N.D.C.C. §§9-08-02 (exculpation), 9-08-03 (penalties), 9-08-04 (liquidated damages) and 9-08-05 (restricting enforcement). See edu-prohibited-lease-terms-nd. | GA: Applies as written. Separately, a landlord may not knowingly and willfully suspend cooling, heat, light or water to a tenant until a dispossessory action is finally disposed of (O.C.G.A. § 44-7-14.1; fine up to $500; `edu-prohibited-practices-ga`). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | NC: Applies as written. Separately, a landlord that bills the tenant for utilities may not disconnect them for nonpayment (N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-42.1(b)). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | SC: Tagged. Voluntary termination of utilities after default in rent makes abandonment immediate (S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-730(b)). | TN: Tagged 2026-09-28 (section text read 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser (Justia host copy of the 2025 Tennessee Code with history lines; 2025-2026 public chapters screened; TN log §1)). Consistent with Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-401 duties; no conflicting statute. TN-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. | VA: Tagged 2026-09-28. VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Read against the official Code of Virginia section-open (law.lis.virginia.gov; VA log §1). Basis: Consistent with Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1227(A)(6). | AL: Tagged. Contract term; the landlord's own essential-service duties are in Ala. Code § 35-9A-204(a)(6) and Ala. Code § 35-9A-404(b). Tampering with meters is a crime (Ala. Code § 13A-8-23). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | PA: Tagged. Consistent with 66 Pa.C.S. Chapter 15 Subchapter B. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | UT: Generic; no conflict. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IL: Tagged. No Illinois statute limits this tenant duty; the landlord's own shutoff ban is 765 ILCS 735/1.4. Read section-open 2026-09-30 (IL log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | ID: Lawful as written. Read section-open 2026-09-30 from legislature.idaho.gov (ID log s1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | MO: Applies as written. The landlord's own willful interruption of essential services is barred by Mo. Rev. Stat. § 441.233(2). Read section-open 2026-09-30 (MO log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IN: Applies as written. A tenant may not interrupt electricity, gas, water or other essential services if it will cause serious damage to the rental unit (Ind. Code § 32-31-5-6(d)). Read section-open 2026-09-30 from iga.in.gov (IN log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | OK: Lease term; the landlord's own willful or negligent failure to supply essential services triggers tenant remedies (Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 121(C)). Read section-open 2026-09-30 to 2026-10-01 from oklegislature.gov (OK log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | MI: Applies as written. Read section-open 2026-10-01 from legislature.mi.gov (MI log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IA: Applies as written.",
