    notes: "CO added - verified this session (statute walk + full-library audit; content itself unchanged WY added 2026-08-21 (full-library cross-check pass): generic mechanics, no CO-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with WY findings from this project. | NE extended (session 2, whole-library generic-clause audit): generic mechanics, no NE-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with NE findings from this project. | MN extended (Minnesota session, whole-library audit): generic mechanics, already vetted against KS/NE's prohibited-lease-provisions statutes (the strictest bar found in this project to date) since this clause was already tagged KS;NE; no MN-specific statutory language or number identified in this session's statute walk that conflicts. No exculpatory/liability-waiver language present. | ND ADDED 2026-09-06 (ND re-audit, exhaustive generic-clause audit prompted by the checklist-to-CSV reconciliation screen). ND's ORIGINAL whole-library audit was written up in its log but largely never executed against the CSV -- ND was shipped 'complete' with 18 displayable LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 61-75 for CO/WY/KS/NE/MN. This row is generic boilerplate carrying no ND-specific statutory interaction; ND's ch. 47-16 was read in full from primary text this session and no conflict was identified. LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK: North Dakota has NO enumerated prohibited-lease-provisions statute (confirmed this session -- § 47-16-02 is a maximum-term cap, and § 47-16-13.3 supplies only case-by-case unconscionability). The exculpation exposure that forced fixes to this clause family in KS and NE therefore does not arise for ND, same reasoning as the WY addendum. 5a.1 JUDGMENT: UNIFORM -- states field changed, clause TEXT unchanged, no re-review owed on existing tags. | SD ADDED 2026-09-07 (SD re-audit, Tier A of the L.2 exhaustive generic-clause audit). SD displayed only 13 LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 60-75 for every other state; 46 generics had no SD tag and no SD override. Triaged per L.2, not bulk-extended. Tier A = boilerplate with no SD statutory interaction, or self-limiting text that defers to applicable law. S5a.1 JUDGMENT: adding a state tag changes `states` only - no bodyText, rule_type or content_type change - so no other tagged state's rendering is affected and NO propagation to other state logs is owed. State-driven, not uniform. AMENDED AND EXTENDED TO CA 2026-09-19: absorbed addendum-precedence-ca, which differed only by the savings clause 'any disclosure, notice, or addendum required by law will control over any conflicting term of this Lease' - true and protective in every state, not CA-specific. The CA override is deleted and this row now serves all nine states — Taylor's 'massage one row to cover several states' rather than keep a near-identical override. THIS CHANGED THE TEXT FOR THE EIGHT EXISTING STATES; the addition is strictly protective and lawful in each, but it is a real edit to their clause, made deliberately. | NV: Read in full 2026-09-24 against NRS 118A (revisor text Rev. 4/15/2026, 2025 session incorporated). Applies as written. | TX: Read in full 2026-09-25 against Tex. Prop. Code ch. 92 (full chapter, section-open; Justia 2025 host copy with per-section history lines). Applies as written. Generic; the statutory-notice carve-out protects the s92.0135 flood notice and s92.016/.0161/.017 statements. | NJ: added 2026-09-26 (tag-first screen, instruction 26). No NJ conflict. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | FL: Applies as written (tag-first screen, instruction 26). Carve-out for legally required addenda covers the §83.505, §83.512 and §83.595 documents. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | AZ: Applies as written. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | ND 2026-09-28: the LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK above is withdrawn as to any clause disclaiming liability for the landlord's own violation of law. North Dakota does have enumerated bans outside its landlord-tenant title: N.D.C.C. §§9-08-02 (exculpation), 9-08-03 (penalties), 9-08-04 (liquidated damages) and 9-08-05 (restricting enforcement). See edu-prohibited-lease-terms-nd. | GA: Applies as written. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | NC: Applies as written. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | SC: Tagged. Generic mechanics; no South Carolina conflict. | TN: Tagged 2026-09-28 (section text read 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser (Justia host copy of the 2025 Tennessee Code with history lines; 2025-2026 public chapters screened; TN log §1)). No conflicting statute. TN-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. | VA: Tagged 2026-09-28. VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Read against the official Code of Virginia section-open (law.lis.virginia.gov; VA log §1). Basis: No conflicting Virginia statute; state-required disclosures control. | AL: Tagged. Where a lease and a rule vary, the lease prevails (Ala. Code § 35-9A-302(c)). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | PA: Tagged. Legally required disclosures control - includes `consumer-restrictions-statement-pa`. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | UT: Generic; no conflict. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IL: Tagged. The required-disclosure carve-out keeps the Summary of Rights (765 ILCS 752/20), flood (765 ILCS 705/25) and radon (420 ILCS 46/26) forms controlling over any conflicting lease term. Read section-open 2026-09-30 (IL log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | ID: No Idaho rule on addendum order found. Lawful as written. Read section-open 2026-09-30 from legislature.idaho.gov (ID log s1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | MO: Applies as written; the required-disclosure carve-out keeps Mo. Rev. Stat. § 535.185, Mo. Rev. Stat. § 441.236 and Mo. Rev. Stat. § 442.055 disclosures (landlord-disclosure-mo, meth-disclosure-mo, contamination-disclosure-mo) controlling. Read section-open 2026-09-30 (MO log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IN: Applies as written. Indiana's prescribed lease disclosures (landlord-disclosure-in, flood-disclosure-in, military-installation-disclosure-in, smoke-detector-acknowledgment-in, water-sewer-billing-disclosure-in) control over conflicting terms under the clause's last limb. Read section-open 2026-09-30 from iga.in.gov (IN log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | OK: Contract term. Read section-open 2026-09-30 to 2026-10-01 from oklegislature.gov (OK log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | MI: Applies as written. Michigan's required lease statements (Mich. Comp. Laws §§ 554.634, 554.601a, 554.603, 559.212(3)), and the optional Mich. Comp. Laws § 554.601b statement where used, control under its 'required by law' exception. Read section-open 2026-10-01 from legislature.mi.gov (MI log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IA: Applies as written. Iowa's required written disclosures (Iowa Code § 562A.13(1), (6); `landlord-disclosure-ia`, `superfund-disclosure-ia`) and the federal lead disclosure control under its 'required by law' exception.",
