    notes: "CO added - verified this session (statute walk + full-library audit; content itself unchanged WY added 2026-08-21 (full-library cross-check pass): generic mechanics, no CO-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with WY findings from this project. | NE extended (session 2, whole-library generic-clause audit): generic mechanics, no NE-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with NE findings from this project. | MN extended (Minnesota session, whole-library audit): generic mechanics, already vetted against KS/NE's prohibited-lease-provisions statutes (the strictest bar found in this project to date) since this clause was already tagged KS;NE; no MN-specific statutory language or number identified in this session's statute walk that conflicts. No exculpatory/liability-waiver language present. | ND ADDED 2026-09-06 (ND re-audit, exhaustive generic-clause audit prompted by the checklist-to-CSV reconciliation screen). ND's ORIGINAL whole-library audit was written up in its log but largely never executed against the CSV -- ND was shipped 'complete' with 18 displayable LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 61-75 for CO/WY/KS/NE/MN. This row is generic boilerplate carrying no ND-specific statutory interaction; ND's ch. 47-16 was read in full from primary text this session and no conflict was identified. LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK: North Dakota has NO enumerated prohibited-lease-provisions statute (confirmed this session -- § 47-16-02 is a maximum-term cap, and § 47-16-13.3 supplies only case-by-case unconscionability). The exculpation exposure that forced fixes to this clause family in KS and NE therefore does not arise for ND, same reasoning as the WY addendum. 5a.1 JUDGMENT: UNIFORM -- states field changed, clause TEXT unchanged, no re-review owed on existing tags. | SD ADDED 2026-09-07 (SD re-audit, Tier A of the L.2 exhaustive generic-clause audit). SD displayed only 13 LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 60-75 for every other state; 46 generics had no SD tag and no SD override. Triaged per L.2, not bulk-extended. Tier A = boilerplate with no SD statutory interaction, or self-limiting text that defers to applicable law. S5a.1 JUDGMENT: adding a state tag changes `states` only - no bodyText, rule_type or content_type change - so no other tagged state's rendering is affected and NO propagation to other state logs is owed. State-driven, not uniform. CA: extended to California 2026-09-19 after re-screen against the full CA pass (the extend manifest had deferred tagging until the blocked set was resolved, and the step was then missed). For a s1947.1 qualifying property (certificate of occupancy on/after 2025-01-01, 16+ units, one of ten named counties) parking may NOT be in the rental agreement - use a separate parking agreement instead. See unbundled-parking-ca. | NV: Read in full 2026-09-24 against NRS 118A (revisor text Rev. 4/15/2026, 2025 session incorporated). Applies as written. | SHARED EDIT 2026-09-25 (TX pass): appended 'subject to any limits applicable law places on changing parking rules or policies during the Term'. Driven by Tex. Prop. Code s92.0131(e). Classification: UNIFORM - self-limiting. Propagation note owed to CO, WY, KS, NE, MN, ND, SD, OH, CA, NV (TX log s16). | TX: Read in full 2026-09-25 against Tex. Prop. Code ch. 92 (full chapter, section-open; Justia 2025 host copy with per-section history lines). Applies as written. Tagged after the uniform edit recorded in this row's notes (s92.0131(e): mid-term parking-rule changes need a listed ground and take effect no sooner than 14 days after notice; s92.0132 permits coterminous with the lease). | NJ: added 2026-09-26 (tag-first screen, instruction 26). No NJ conflict found. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | FL: Applies as written (tag-first screen, instruction 26). Generic; no Florida parking-rule-change statute in Part II. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | AZ: Applies as written. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | ND 2026-09-28: the LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK above is withdrawn as to any clause disclaiming liability for the landlord's own violation of law. North Dakota does have enumerated bans outside its landlord-tenant title: N.D.C.C. §§9-08-02 (exculpation), 9-08-03 (penalties), 9-08-04 (liquidated damages) and 9-08-05 (restricting enforcement). See edu-prohibited-lease-terms-nd. | GA: Applies as written. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | NC: Applies as written. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | SC: Tagged. Generic; no South Carolina statute. | TN: Tagged 2026-09-28 (section text read 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser (Justia host copy of the 2025 Tennessee Code with history lines; 2025-2026 public chapters screened; TN log §1)). No conflicting statute. TN-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. | VA: Tagged 2026-09-28. VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Read against the official Code of Virginia section-open (law.lis.virginia.gov; VA log §1). Basis: No conflicting statute; reassignment agreed in the lease is not a unilateral change under Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1204(I); accessible-parking requests are accommodation requests (Va. Code Ann. § 36-96.3:2(B)). | AL: Tagged. No conflicting statute. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | PA: Tagged. No statute. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | UT: Generic; no Utah parking-rule statute for residential leases located. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IL: Tagged. No Illinois statute on assigned parking in residential leases located; a required parking charge is a non-optional fee listed on page 1 (765 ILCS 705/35(b)). The fee law applies to leases entered into after its effective date (January 1, 2027 in official records; the Act's text says July 1, 2026; IL log §1.2). Read section-open 2026-09-30 (IL log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | ID: No Idaho statute limits changing parking assignments. Lawful as written. Read section-open 2026-09-30 from legislature.idaho.gov (ID log s1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | MO: Applies as written. No Missouri statute limits changes to parking assignments; towing from the property is governed by Mo. Rev. Stat. § 304.157(4) (edu-towing-mo). Read section-open 2026-09-30 (MO log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IN: Applies as written. No Indiana statute limits changes to a tenant's assigned parking. Read section-open 2026-09-30 from iga.in.gov (IN log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | OK: Lease term; no Oklahoma statute limits changes to parking assignments. Read section-open 2026-09-30 to 2026-10-01 from oklegislature.gov (OK log §1). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | IA: Applies as written; no Iowa statute limits reassigning a parking space (IA log §17).",
