    lastChecked: "2026-10-01",
    topicKey: "repair-notice",
    notes: "CO: CITED — C.R.S. § 38-12-503(3)(f)(II), (3)(e); Anderson v. Shorter Arms Investors, LLC, 2023 COA 71, 537 P.3d 831. Corrected 2026-08-27: a bracket prompt suggesting a phone number as the notice channel would have waived the landlord's own right to written notice under (3)(f)(II); rewritten written-only with a warning. (Restored 2026-09-25 from lease-clause-citations-CO.csv, which still holds the same data.) | CO: SCRUB 2026-09-29 (checklist instruction 66, three-bucket test): kept the written-notice channel, which protects the landlord's right to written notice; restated warranty and retaliation sentences removed (edu-written-notice-strictly-required-co, edu-retaliation-co). | CO: CO retro (SOP 1.16) 2026-10-01, rule 40 (also rules 42, 44, 46). FIXED - this clause did not satisfy C.R.S. § 38-12-505(3)(d), which since 2025-01-01 requires EVERY rental agreement to include, \"in English and Spanish and in at least twelve-point, bold-faced type\", a statement giving BOTH (i) an address where a tenant can mail or personally deliver written notice of an uninhabitable condition AND (ii) an email address or accessible online tenant portal for the same notice. Statute read section-open in the official 2026 C.R.S. (Colorado OLLS whole-title HTM, olls.info/crs/crs2026-title-38.htm / -13 / -24 / -06 / -00); added by SB 24-094, ch. 158, p. 713, § 5, eff. 2024-05-03, lease duty operative 2025-01-01. Four defects fixed: rule_type was RECOMMENDED for a REQUIRED statement; no Spanish; only one channel where the statute requires two; and the 2026-09-29 three-bucket scrub had removed the warranty/retaliation sentences that § 38-12-505(3)(c) separately requires in the lease (restored as the new row habitability-rights-statement-co). The written-only warning is kept: § 38-12-503(3)(f)(II) still waives the landlord's right to written notice if the lease designates a verbal method. RENDERING REQUIREMENT for the builder: this clause must print in at least 12-point bold-faced type. The Spanish text is Claude's translation, not a state-prescribed form (the statute prescribes content, language and type size, not wording) - flagged for Taylor.",
