    notes: "WY added 2026-08-21. Citation: W.S. 1-21-1207. Source: law.justia.com/codes/wyoming/title-1/chapter-21/article-12/section-1-21-1207/. Genuine REQUIRED disclosure — satisfies bucket-test criterion #1. Note: statute requires this be stated in the agreement AND separately, in writing, at the time the deposit is collected — this clause satisfies the first prong only; the second is a process step, logged separately as edu-nonrefundable-deposit-separate-notice-wy so it isn't lost. | WY: RETRO 2026-09-30 (SOP 1.15, rule 42). W.S. 1-21-1207 read section-open 2026-09-30: 'Any rental agreement shall state WHETHER any portion of a deposit is nonrefundable'. The duty runs on every Wyoming rental agreement that takes a deposit, including one with no nonrefundable portion, so the row stays REQUIRED rather than CONDITIONAL. Text rewritten because the old wording asserted that '$0 ... is nonrefundable and will not be returned to Tenant regardless of the condition of the property', which reads as a nonsense assertion in the (common) $0 case and left the statutory 'whether' answered only by a parenthetical aside. New wording states the answer affirmatively either way. Rule 40 note: the section prescribes no type size, bold, underline or placement, and no sanction attaches to omitting it -- W.S. 1-21-1208(c)'s penalty reaches only subsections (a) and (b) of 1-21-1208, not 1-21-1207. Read section-open 2026-09-30 from the official Wyoming Legislature NXT gateway, 2026 Wyoming Statutes (wyoleg.gov/NXT/gateway.dll/2026 Wyoming Statutes/2026 Titles/1/53/...); Article 12 text confirmed identical in the 2024 and 2026 editions.",
