    notes: "TX: Tex. Prop. Code ch. 92 read in full, section-open, 2026-09-25 (Justia '2025 Texas Statutes' host copy supplied by Taylor; per-section history lines checked - latest amendments 89th Leg., R.S. (2025); CONFIRMED 2026-09-25 against the official statutes.capitol.texas.gov ch. 92 page supplied by Taylor: no 1st or 2nd called-session amendment; text matches section for section - TX log s14). Controlling text: ss92.201-.208 (Subch. E; Amended by Acts 1995, 74th Leg., ch. 869, eff. Jan. 1, 1996) and s92.003. Texas does NOT require the disclosure at lease signing - it is triggered by a tenant's (or official's) request (s92.201(b)(1)-(2)) - but s92.201(b)(3) treats inclusion in the lease before any request as full compliance, which takes the landlord out of the s92.202 request-and-notice liability track. Correction duty s92.203; willful misstatement is bad faith regardless of rent delinquency (s92.204, s92.206). Owner address may be street OR post-office box; management company needs a STREET address (s92.201(a)). Assumed name allowed if a certificate is recorded (s92.201(f)). Bonus (s92.003(b)): written notice of the management company's name and business street address makes the management company the owner's SOLE agent for service of process. Duties non-waivable (s92.006(a)); remedies s92.205 (one month's rent + $100, costs, fees, unilateral termination). Local ordinances may add enforcement only (s92.208).",
