    notes: "TX: Primary text supplied by Taylor 2026-09-25 from the official Texas Constitution and Statutes site (statutes.capitol.texas.gov), with per-section history lines; read section-open. Controlling text: Tex. Prop. Code ss54.041-.048 (Subch. C; s54.046 Amended by Acts 2015, 84th Leg., R.S., Ch. 1198 (S.B. 1367), eff. Jan. 1, 2016). The lease must separately AUTHORIZE seizure (s54.044(a)), packing/removal/storage charges (s54.044(c)) and sale (s54.045(a)); the clause does all three. LAYOUT REQUIREMENT - whole lien provision underlined or conspicuous bold (s54.043(a)); without it the lien is unenforceable. Offered, not defaulted (judgment call, TX log s11.5): willful violation costs actual damages + return of property or proceeds + one month's rent + $1,000 + fees (s54.046), and 'without a breach of the peace' is a practice standard no document can guarantee - same class as ND's dormancy-charge limb (b), Addendum M.7. Surplus sale proceeds must be mailed within 30 days; accounting within 30 days of written request (s54.045(d)). Tenant may replevy by bond (s54.048). Contrast NV, where household-goods liens are abolished (edu-landlord-lien-abolished-nv).",
