    notes: "NJ: Primary text read section-open 2026-09-26 from the official N.J.S.A. text supplied by Taylor (lis.njleg.state.nj.us), with per-section chapter-law history lines. Supersedes holdover. Neither holdover nor holdover-ca tagged NJ: base 'double the Monthly Rent' matches neither NJ statute (K.3); holdover-ca's 'terminable only as provided by law' is safe but omits NJ's double-rent rights (ceiling-only forfeit, K.3). Controlling text: 46:8-10 (month-to-month on acceptance of rent, absent agreement); 2A:42-5 (tenant who gives notice to quit and stays: DOUBLE THE RENT for the whole holdover); 2A:42-6 (willful holdover after term + written demand: DOUBLE THE YEARLY VALUE for the detention period); 2A:18-61.3(a) (no eviction or NON-RENEWAL except for good cause in covered premises); Anti-Eviction exemption 2A:18-61.1 (owner-occupied premises with not more than two rental units; transient/seasonal; certain family-member trust units). NEEDS_REVIEW: how 2A:42-5 and 2A:42-6 interact with the Anti-Eviction Act for covered tenants is a case-law question not read; the clause hedges 2A:42-5 and confines 2A:42-6 to exempt premises pending that. Builder: this row is CONDITIONAL on property type (Anti-Eviction coverage). | NJ: research pass 2026-09-26 (advanced research, report in conversation): Lorril Co. v. La Corte, 352 N.J. Super. 433 (App. Div. 2002) applied 2A:42-5 to residential tenants who gave notice and stayed (double rent only for days actually in possession). No case found on 2A:42-6 vs Anti-Eviction Act coverage; clause already confines 2A:42-6 to exempt premises. Stays NEEDS_REVIEW on that interaction only. | NJ: CLOSED 2026-09-26. NEEDS_REVIEW cleared on the ground that the clause makes no claim the open question could falsify: it asserts N.J.S.A. 2A:42-6 only where the Anti-Eviction Act does NOT apply (statute text read), and asserts 2A:42-5 'to the extent [it] applies' - which Lorril Co. v. La Corte, 352 N.J. Super. 433 (App. Div. 2002) applied to residential tenants who gave notice and stayed. The unresolved case-law point (2A:42-6 against covered tenants) is therefore outside the clause, matching the research-pass recommendation not to rely on 2A:42-6 against covered tenants. | NJ: SCRUB 2026-09-29 (checklist instruction 66, three-bucket test): kept the month-to-month continuation and the landlord's double-rent remedies; the tenant's Anti-Eviction Act protection moved to edu-anti-eviction-act-nj.",
