    notes: "NJ: Primary text read section-open 2026-09-26 from the official N.J.S.A. text supplied by Taylor (lis.njleg.state.nj.us), with per-section chapter-law history lines. Controlling text: N.J.S.A. 46:8-50(a), (b), (e), (f), (g) (amended 2023, c.93). Notice before signing or renewal; in a written residential lease it may be included only as a SEPARATE RIDER, individually signed or acknowledged, not less than 12-point type; DCA model notice with 'Flood Risk' heading; FEMA-zone questions may not offer 'unknown'. Remedy: tenant who later learns of undisclosed FEMA-zone location may terminate by written notice, effective on surrender, with refund of prepaid rent within 30 days; damages if flooding harms property, habitability or access. Exempt: seasonal <120 days; landlord definition in (g). Drafting defect recorded: (f) refers to 'subsection f.' but plainly means (e). NEEDS_REVIEW: (1) the DCA model notice itself (published in the N.J. Register) not read - questions above track the statute's 'substantially similar language'; (2) (d) says the duty to disclose FEMA-zone status 'beyond actual knowledge' takes effect only after the DEP address look-up tool is in place - whether it is live not verified. LAYOUT: separate signed rider, 12-point minimum, heading text (instruction 28). | NJ: research pass 2026-09-26 (advanced research, report in conversation): DCA model 'Flood Risk Notice' posted 2023-12-21 (nj.gov/dca/codes/offices/pdf/Flood_Risk_Notice.pdf) - answers include 'Yes-effective map / Yes-preliminary map / No' for FEMA-zone questions; DEP Flood Risk Notification Tool (flooddisclosure.nj.gov) live since 2023-12-21, so the beyond-actual-knowledge FEMA duty is IN EFFECT; DCA says obligation began 2024-03-20. Stays NEEDS_REVIEW until the rider body is aligned to the DCA model form text (answer options differ from this draft). | NJ: 2026-09-26 body REPLACED with the DCA model Flood Risk Notice text VERBATIM (nj.gov/dca/codes/offices/pdf/Flood_Risk_Notice.pdf, 2 pages, pasted by Taylor; posted 2023-12-21 per research pass). FEMA-zone questions offer 'Yes, effective map / Yes, preliminary map / No' - no 'Unknown', as 46:8-50(b) requires; question 3 allows Unknown. Form adds block/lot, event descriptions, dated signatures of both parties, the climate note, and repeats the (c) flood-insurance text. DEP look-up tool (flooddisclosure.nj.gov) live since 2023-12-21, so FEMA-zone disclosure beyond actual knowledge is in effect (46:8-50(d)); DCA says the obligation began 2024-03-20. Model-notice N.J. Register cite not found (form is from DCA's website). Builder: new placeholders {{property_address}}, {{municipality}}, {{county}}, {{block}}, {{lot}}. NEEDS_REVIEW cleared.",
