    notes: "NJ: N.J.A.C. 5:10 read section-open 2026-09-26 from the nj.gov OAL compilation supplied by Taylor, stamped 'adopted and published through 55 N.J.R. (Aug. 7, 2023)'. Currency beyond that stamp asserted only by spot-check against the Cornell LII copy (updated quarterly; last amendment shown R.2023 d.089, eff. 2023-08-07) and one web search finding no later 5:10 adoption touching this section (instruction 16). Controlling text: N.J.A.C. 5:10-14.4(c) (amended R.2023 d.089): in a multiple dwelling the owner must supply heating fuel or energy 'notwithstanding any contractual provision seeking to delegate or shift responsibility to the occupant', EXCEPT where the occupant 'agrees in writing to supply heat to his own unit' AND the unit has its own exclusive heating equipment whose heat source can be separately computed and billed. Owner keeps the maintenance duty (14.4(c)). An occupant who by lease heats OTHER units becomes responsible like an owner (5:10-5.6(a)). Heat standard: 68F 6am-11pm and 65F 11pm-6am, October 1 to May 15 (5:10-14.4(a), May 15 since 2023-08-07); owner not liable for heat loss from tenant leaving windows or doors open (14.4(b)). CONDITIONAL on tenant-paid heat in a multiple dwelling.",
