    notes: "NJ: Text read 2026-09-26 from the Justia host copy of N.J.S.A. (fetched by me, not pasted); history lines checked; not compared against the official site (instruction 29 caveat). Supersedes returned-payments (base not tagged NJ). Why an override: the base caps its fee at 'the maximum amount permitted by applicable law' and NJ has NO such cap located - an empty referent (K.3); the NJ row states the fee as a lease figure instead. Controlling text: N.J.S.A. 2A:32A-1 (L.1993, c.379, s.1; amended 2014, c.46) is a PAYEE REMEDY, not a fee cap: a maker who fails to pay within 35 days after a certified-mail demand is liable for the face amount plus attorneys' fees, court costs, mailing costs and damages of the greater of $100 or TRIPLE the amount (the section also prescribes bilingual demand-notice wording and lets the court waive damages for hardship - those subsections summarized by the host, not read verbatim). Covers electronic funds transfers too (2014 amendment). Replacement-payment methods listed are non-electronic, consistent with N.J.S.A. 46:8-49.1 (landlord may not require EFT). The fee is not labeled 'additional rent' (Taylor decision 2026-09-26), so it cannot support a nonpayment eviction. Reasonableness of the fee amount is case law, not read; builder may warn on high values. CLOSES the held row.",
