    lastChecked: "2026-09-29",
    topicKey: "security-deposit-return",
    notes: "FL: Primary text read section-open 2026-09-26 from the official 2026 Florida Statutes (flsenate.gov / leg.state.fl.us), with per-section history lines. Instruction 24 family closed for FL: supersedes the blank-states parent (M.11). Controlling text: Fla. Stat. §83.49 (last amended s. 2, ch. 2024-199; s. 2, ch. 2025-16 added e-mail delivery under §83.505, eff. 2025-07-01 per Laws of Fla. ch. 2025-16). Holding methods and interest: §83.49(1)(a)-(c) (five-or-more-county landlords may post one Secretary of State bond, $250,000 cap; county bond cap $50,000). Annual interest: §83.49(9). Return: §83.49(3)(a) 15 days if no claim; claim notice within 30 days by certified mail or §83.505 e-mail with the prescribed form; forfeiture of the claim (not of the damages action) if late. Objection and remittance: §83.49(3)(b). Fees: §83.49(3)(c) prevailing party, and §83.48 (non-waivable). Tenant's 7-day vacate notice: §83.49(5) ('Except when otherwise provided by the terms of a written rental agreement'). Renewal: §83.49(6). Transfer: §83.49(7) (rebuttable presumption new owner received the deposit, limited to 1 month's rent). Scope: §83.49(4) excludes transient hotel/motel rentals and rentals whose rent or deposit is regulated by law or a public body (public housing, s. 8 and similar programs, other than rent stabilization); housing authorities are bound only by (3), (5) and (6). §83.49(3)(d): compliance with §83.49 satisfies all other Florida deposit statutes (incl. ch. 475 brokers). NO deposit cap in Part II (full read). Deadline runs from termination of the rental agreement. The claim-notice form text is in §83.49(3)(a) and goes in the builder's move-out workflow, not the lease. Builder: require {{deposit_holding_method}}; if (b) or (c), interest must be disclosed in security-deposit-notice-fl. The deposit-alternative option is fee-in-lieu-of-deposit-fl (not a security deposit, §83.491(6)). | FL: SCRUB 2026-09-29 (checklist instruction 66, three-bucket test): kept the landlord's holding-method choice and the tenant's 7-day vacating-notice duty; the restated handling, claim-notice, objection, return and transfer rules moved to edu-security-deposit-rules-fl.",
