    notes: "FL: Primary text read section-open 2026-09-26 from the official 2026 Florida Statutes (flsenate.gov / leg.state.fl.us), with per-section history lines. Supersedes pet-policy (base not tagged FL). Why an override: the base lets the landlord 'enter the property and remove a pet, without liability to Tenant' in several situations. Pet removal is not an entry purpose in Fla. Stat. §83.53 beyond emergency or protection and preservation, removing tenant property outside surrender, abandonment or lawful eviction is barred by §83.67(5), and 'without liability' purports to limit landlord liability arising under law (void under §83.47(1)(b); actual damages for inclusion under §83.47(2)). A pet deposit is 'deposit money' (§83.43(4)) and so falls under §83.49 holding, notice and return rules. 'Pet rent' is labeled rent, so it is 'rent' under §83.43(12) (designated as rent in writing); that differs from late fees, which the library does not label rent. The indemnity sentence is not written to cover Landlord's own negligence. No Florida pet-specific landlord statute located in Part II. Assistance animals: instruction 24 family, see the FL log.",
