  "assistance-animal-accommodation-fl": {
    ruleTypes: ["REQUIRED"],
    contentType: "LEASE_CLAUSE",
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    effectiveFrom: "2026-09-26",
    lastChecked: "2026-09-26",
    topicKey: "assistance-animal-accommodation",
    notes: "FL: Primary text pasted by Taylor 2026-09-26 from flsenate.gov/Laws/Statutes/2026 (official 2026 Florida Statutes), read section-open with history lines. Instruction 24 family closed for FL: supersedes assistance-animal-accommodation (base tagged KS;NV;TX, not FL). Why an override: the base's direct-threat denial reaches every assistance animal, but Florida's service-animal housing rule has no such limit (Fla. Stat. §413.08(6)(b): 'full and equal access to all housing accommodations', no extra compensation, liable for damage, 'may request proof of compliance with vaccination requirements'); the direct-threat exclusion in §413.08(3)(f) is for public accommodations only. Emotional support animals: Fla. Stat. §760.27 (s. 1, ch. 2020-76): kept 'upon the person's request and approval by a housing provider'; no extra compensation; denial only for a direct threat to safety or health of others or of physical damage to the property of others (§760.27(2)(a)); documentation of disability ((2)(b)1-5) and of need for the particular animal ((2)(c)) when not readily apparent; per-animal need ((2)(d)); licensing and vaccination proof ((2)(e)); no diagnosis, severity or medical records ((3)(a)); no required form or notarized statement, no denial solely for not using the routine method ((3)(b)); Internet registrations insufficient alone ((3)(c)); tenant liable for damage ((4)). §760.27 does not apply to service animals ((5)); §413.08(6)(b) does not apply to ESAs. CLASSIFICATION: Florida has an independent, animal-specific housing statute for SERVICE animals (§413.08(6), with a criminal penalty in (7)) and a separate ESA statute; §760.27(2)'s nondiscrimination sentence is tied to federal law ('To the extent required by federal law, rule, or regulation'), so the federal-guidance caveat (HUD withdrawal 2025-09-17; enforcement narrowed 2026-05-22) carries into the ESA half; the no-extra-compensation and documentation limits are stated without that qualifier. Service-animal definition §413.08(1)(d): the dog-or-miniature-horse limit applies only to subsections (2)-(4) (public accommodations), not to (6) housing. SCOPE SPLIT (ref 294.7): §760.29(1)(a) exempts from §760.27 a single-family house rented by an owner of no more than three without a licensee, and owner-occupied buildings of four or fewer units; §413.08's 'housing accommodation' excludes only a single-family residence renting no more than one room (§413.08(1)(a)). Builder: the clause is safe to include even where §760.27 does not apply. Practitioner definitions (§§456.001, 456.47) not read (L.5).",
  },
