    notes: "AZ: Read section-open 2026-09-26/27 in the browser from azleg.gov (official legislative compilation, stated as updated through the 57th Legislature, 2nd Regular Session, 2026). azleg ARS pages print no history lines, so currency rests on the compilation date and the session-law check in the AZ log (s1.1). OPT-IN LANDLORD RIGHT (instruction 30): A.R.S. §33-1314(E) 'the landlord may request and the tenant may provide and routinely update the name and contact information of a person who is authorized by the tenant to enter...'. Without it, the landlord falls back on §33-1370 and may release an animal to a relative only in the §33-1314(E)(1)-(3) cases. Controlling text: A.R.S. §33-1314(E) (contact failure: 1 day for an animal, 10 days for other property; dispose under §33-1370 or deem the animal abandoned and release it under §33-1370(E); relative release), (F) (government-issued identification; 20 days after first written contact or the last paid-rent date, whichever is longer; no further landlord liability once the authorized person removes possessions; leftover property under §33-1370), (G) (scope: property only if rent unpaid 5+ days; animal only if the tenant is deceased or incapacitated). The no-liability sentence restates a statutory immunity; it is not a lease exculpation (§33-1315(A)(3)). §33-1314(E) opens with 'Notwithstanding section 14-3911' (probate) - §14-3911 NOT read (L.5 dependency).",
