    notes: "AZ: Read section-open 2026-09-26/27 in the browser from azleg.gov (official legislative compilation, stated as updated through the 57th Legislature, 2nd Regular Session, 2026). azleg ARS pages print no history lines, so currency rests on the compilation date and the session-law check in the AZ log (s1.1). Controlling text: A.R.S. §33-1324(C) (single family residence: agreement in writing, supported by adequate consideration, in good faith and not to evade, may shift the (A)(5) and (A)(6) duties and specified repairs, maintenance tasks, alterations and remodeling, but not work needed to cure (A)(1)-(2) noncompliance), (D) (any other dwelling unit: only if in good faith, SET FORTH IN A SEPARATE WRITING SIGNED BY THE PARTIES and supported by adequate consideration; not (A)(1)-(2) work; does not diminish obligations to other tenants). WHY THIS ROW EXISTS: landscaping-irrigation and snow-removal assign maintenance tasks to the tenant inside the lease, with no separate signed writing and no stated consideration, which fails §33-1324(D) for any unit other than a single family residence. TAYLOR'S DECISION (2026-09-27): tag both shared rows AZ for single family residences only (product gap flagged for Claude CLI) and use this separate AZ agreement for every other unit; their text is kept in the first two checkboxes for that case. Instruction 28: separate-writing requirement (non-SFR). 'Single family residence' per §33-1310(16). Compare maintenance-allocation-fl (FL allows modification in writing for single-family and duplex only).",
