  "security-deposit-return-tn-act": {
    ruleTypes: ["REQUIRED"],
    contentType: "LEASE_CLAUSE",
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    effectiveFrom: "2026-09-28",
    lastChecked: "2026-09-29",
    topicKey: "security-deposit-return",
    notes: "TN: TN-SCOPE: ACT COUNTIES ONLY (pair with security-deposit-return-tn-other, choice group tn-urlta-deposit-return; default). Instruction 24 REQUIRED family. Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser from Justia's host copy of the 2025 Tennessee Code (the official code is published by LexisNexis), with each section's history line; currency checked against the full text of every public chapter of the 114th General Assembly (2025 and 2026 Pub. Ch. 1 to 1142 and the seven 2025 First Extraordinary Session acts, publications.tnsosfiles.com) and against the LexisNexis Tennessee Code Unannotated free public access site, which already prints the 2026 Pub. Ch. 606 sections (TN log §1). Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-301 (history ends Acts 2012, ch. 887, § 1): (a) separate account at a state- or federally-regulated institution; (h) 'all landlords' must tell tenants at signing and deposit where the account is, but not the account number; (b)(1)(A) notice of the right to be present, inspection on the vacate day or within 4 calendar days, and the no-show waiver - which binds only if 'notice of the tenant's waiver ... is set out in the rental agreement', so this clause carries it (opt-in landlord right, instruction 30); (b)(1)(B) signed list conclusive except (g); (b)(2) the seven no-inspection grounds and certificate-of-mailing copy on written request; (c) FORFEITURE: no landlord may retain any part of the deposit if it was not in the separate account AND the listing was not provided (omission sanction, instruction 28); (e) application to unpaid rent; (f) refund notice and 60-day retention; (g) later-discovered damage, 30 days / 7 days. Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-305: seller released after good-faith sale, written notice and transfer of the deposit. NO RETURN DEADLINE, NO CAP, NO INTEREST, NO ITEMIZATION DEADLINE in Tennessee law (see edu-security-deposit-rules-tn, edu-no-deposit-cap-tn, edu-no-deposit-interest-tn); the 'promptly when Tenant responds' promise is contractual. The statute says the landlord 'may' give the right-to-be-present notice; the clause commits to giving it because the waiver and the forfeiture protection both depend on it. OPEN (not blocking): Tennessee's Unclaimed Property Act lists 'security deposit' as reportable property (Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-29-102(24)(B)(ii)); how that interacts with § 66-28-301(f)'s 60-day retention right was not resolved (TN log §7). COUNTY-LAYER PILOT (Taylor, 2026-09-28): Tennessee is the test case for the future county/local layer. The URLTA (Tenn. Code Ann. Title 66, Chapter 28) applies only in the 17 counties over 75,000 people in the 2010 census, a list frozen by 2021 Pub. Ch. 182 § 2 (Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-102(a)): Anderson, Blount, Bradley, Davidson, Hamilton, Knox, Madison, Maury, Montgomery, Rutherford, Sevier, Shelby, Sullivan, Sumner, Washington, Williamson and Wilson. | TN: SCRUB 2026-09-29 (checklist instruction 66, three-bucket test): removed only the restated duty to inspect without the tenant; the account-location statement, inspection notice, the waiver warning the statute requires in the lease, and the landlord's rights stay (edu-security-deposit-rules-tn).",
  },
