    topicKey: "alarm-duties",
    notes: "TN: TN-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser from Justia's host copy of the 2025 Tennessee Code (the official code is published by LexisNexis), with each section's history line; currency checked against the full text of every public chapter of the 114th General Assembly (2025 and 2026 Pub. Ch. 1 to 1142 and the seven 2025 First Extraordinary Session acts, publications.tnsosfiles.com) and against the LexisNexis Tennessee Code Unannotated free public access site, which already prints the 2026 Pub. Ch. 606 sections (TN log §1). Outside the landlord-tenant title (gap-discovery source 4). Tenn. Code Ann. § 68-102-151 (Acts 2005, ch. 148; 2015, ch. 120): unlawful to own or operate a ONE- OR TWO-FAMILY rental unit (house, cottage, duplex or condominium) without an approved smoke alarm in each living unit, audible in the sleeping rooms; (d)(1) the TENANT maintains it per the manufacturer's instructions, and on termination of a tenancy the OWNER ensures it is operational before reoccupancy; tampering or removal unlawful; Class A misdemeanor, each day a separate offense. Tenn. Code Ann. § 68-120-112 (2015, ch. 120 and ch. 318): same duty for APARTMENT BUILDINGS of 3 or more units (excluding condominium projects) existing before 2016-01-01; newer buildings follow the building code adopted under § 68-120-101; tenant maintains, owner ensures operational before reoccupancy; Class C misdemeanor. Standards incorporated by reference (UL listing, state fire marshal building standards) - not read (L.5, instruction 16). No carbon monoxide duty for rentals: edu-no-co-alarm-duty-tn. COUNTY-LAYER PILOT (Taylor, 2026-09-28): Tennessee is the test case for the future county/local layer. The URLTA (Tenn. Code Ann. Title 66, Chapter 28) applies only in the 17 counties over 75,000 people in the 2010 census, a list frozen by 2021 Pub. Ch. 182 § 2 (Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-102(a)): Anderson, Blount, Bradley, Davidson, Hamilton, Knox, Madison, Maury, Montgomery, Rutherford, Sevier, Shelby, Sullivan, Sumner, Washington, Williamson and Wilson.",
