    lastChecked: "2026-09-28",
    topicKey: "fee-in-lieu-of-deposit",
    notes: "VA: VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. OPT-IN (instruction 30). Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser on the official Code of Virginia (law.lis.virginia.gov; Title 55.1 Chapter 12 read whole from the vacodefull page, which prints the 2026-session amendments and every delayed-effective version with its history line); 2024-2026 amending chapters read in enrolled text on lis.virginia.gov with their effective-date clauses (VA log §1). Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1226(I)-(J) (five criteria; tenant may switch to the full deposit at any time without consent; landlord shall not alter lease terms if the tenant does); Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1206(A) (landlord may require damage insurance and premiums as a condition of tenancy; premiums are rent, not deposit; written notice of the right to a separate policy; landlord-obtained coverage must insure the tenant; actual cost plus administrative and opt-out fees; summary or certificate before execution; a tenant opting out may provide own policy or pay the full deposit); Va. Code Ann. §§ 55.1-1206(C), 55.1-1208(A)(7) (deposit plus premiums prepaid before commencement capped at two months' rent). Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1200 ('Damage insurance' definition). Form 200 (Rev. 07/23) § 3(g) carries a similar landlord-provided damage insurance program with opt-out fee.",
