    notes: "VA: VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser on the official Code of Virginia (law.lis.virginia.gov; Title 55.1 Chapter 12 read whole from the vacodefull page, which prints the 2026-session amendments and every delayed-effective version with its history line); 2024-2026 amending chapters read in enrolled text on lis.virginia.gov with their effective-date clauses (VA log §1). Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1240, both versions read: (effective until 2027-01-01) either party may terminate; tenant vacates and gives notice within 14 days; landlord 14 days' notice on its determination; deposit and prepaid rent with accrued interest returned unless the landlord reasonably believes the tenant side caused it; proration as of the casualty; 'If continued occupancy is lawful, § 55.1-1411 shall apply' (reasonable reduction of rent, a Chapter 14 cross-reference read section-open). 2026 Acts ch. 1117 (HB 834), 'effective on January 1, 2027' by its second enactment clause, read in enrolled text: tenant notice within 21 days; landlord 21 days' notice only after meeting or a reasonable effort to meet, and offering an available substantially similar unit in the same complex on current terms, OR on a determination that the tenant's § 55.1-1227 violation caused the damage; tenant may request reevaluation within seven days. The clause states both regimes by date so it stays correct across 2027-01-01 (instruction 34). Tenant-side condemnation remedy: Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1243.2 (edu-landlord-repair-duties-va). Form 200 (Rev. 07/23) § 11 adds a casualty release and subrogation waiver that Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1208(A)(5) prohibits (VA log §15). | VA: SCRUB 2026-09-29 (checklist instruction 66, three-bucket test): kept the landlord's termination right with its 2027 conditions; the tenant's options and the deposit and rent rules moved to edu-casualty-termination-va.",
