  "assistance-animal-accommodation-va": {
    ruleTypes: ["REQUIRED"],
    contentType: "LEASE_CLAUSE",
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    effectiveFrom: "2026-09-28",
    lastChecked: "2026-09-28",
    topicKey: "assistance-animal-accommodation",
    notes: "VA: VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Outside-title sections read section-open 2026-09-28 from the official Code of Virginia Law Library compilation (law.lis.virginia.gov/law-library, per-title CSV) overlaid with every section on the official 2026 Updates pages (VA log §17). Virginia Fair Housing Law: Va. Code Ann. § 36-96.1:1 ('Assistance animal' definition, including emotional support; not required to be individually trained or certified; not a pet; 'Disability'); Va. Code Ann. § 36-96.3:1 (2017 cc. 575, 729; 2023 c. 439): (A) comply with rules applicable to all residents that do not interfere; no pet fee, deposit or additional rent; responsible for physical damages if residents with pets are; (B) no additional verification where disability or need is obvious or known; (C) reliable documentation including from a therapeutic relationship; (D) evaluate; (E) 'therapeutic relationship' defined; (F) fraudulent supporting documentation by a provider is a prohibited practice under the Virginia Consumer Protection Act (§ 59.1-200, not read); Va. Code Ann. § 36-96.3:2 (2017 cc. 575, 729; 2021, Sp. Sess. I, c. 17): reasonable-accommodation standard, interactive process, grounds for denial, the clear-and-present-threat test 'not solely based on breed, size, or type'; accessible parking requests are accommodation requests; Va. Code Ann. § 36-96.3(B)(ii). Va. Code Ann. § 51.5-45 (Virginians with Disabilities Act, found by the adjacent-section sweep, L.12): (B) every person with a guide dog, hearing dog or service dog 'shall be entitled to full and equal access with such dog to all housing accommodations' and 'shall not be required to pay extra compensation for such dog but shall be liable for any damage done to the premises by such dog'; (C) no duty to modify property or rent to a direct threat; remedies § 51.5-46 (injunction, compensatory damages, prevailing-party fees; claim notice within 180 days). No Virginia statute makes a tenant's misrepresentation of an assistance animal in housing a crime or a lease default: search '(assistance|service|support) (animal|dog)' within 250 characters of 'misrepresent|fraudulent|false|falsely' returned only § 51.5-44.1 (Class 4 misdemeanor for fraudulently representing a service or hearing dog to gain PUBLIC access under § 51.5-44, not housing); § 36-96.3:1(F) reaches documentation providers (VA log §17). FEDERAL: Fair Housing Act (42 U.S.C. § 3604(f)), not relied on; the HUD guidance history (withdrawn 2025-09-17, enforcement narrowed 2026-05-22) does not affect Virginia's independent statutory definition. INSTRUCTION 24: REQUIRED family closed for VA by this override (base row not tagged). Pet rows: pet-policy-va, pet-insurance-requirement (tagged; excludes assistance animals). Form 200 (Rev. 07/23) § 14 lets the landlord bar all animals 'except for qualified service animals', which understates the statute (VA log §15).",
  },
