    notes: "AL: Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser from the official Code of Alabama 1975 on ALISON (alison.legislature.state.al.us, the Legislature's own code service; Title 35 Chapter 9A read whole, all 48 section numbers, with every history line; newest Chapter 9A amendment Act 2018-473; whole Code loaded, 49,638 section versions including versions effective 2026-10-01 and later; every 2024, 2025 and 2026 act touching landlord-tenant terms screened; AL log §1). Controlling text: Ala. Code § 35-9A-202(a) (landlord or anyone authorized to enter into a rental agreement on its behalf 'shall disclose to the tenant in writing at or before the commencement of the tenancy the name and business address of' the manager and an owner or service/notice agent); Ala. Code § 35-9A-202(b) (kept current; enforceable against successors); Ala. Code § 35-9A-202(c) (a person who fails to comply becomes the landlord's agent for service and notices and for performing the landlord's obligations, including spending rent collected on them). No bar on suit for noncompliance (contrast MN § 504B.181). Out-of-state landlords may be served under Alabama Rule of Civil Procedure 4 (Ala. Code § 35-9A-123(b)). Timing: at or before commencement (instruction 28 timing rule, AL log §4).",
