    notes: "AL: Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser from the official Code of Alabama 1975 on ALISON (alison.legislature.state.al.us, the Legislature's own code service; Title 35 Chapter 9A read whole, all 48 section numbers, with every history line; newest Chapter 9A amendment Act 2018-473; whole Code loaded, 49,638 section versions including versions effective 2026-10-01 and later; every 2024, 2025 and 2026 act touching landlord-tenant terms screened; AL log §1). OPT-IN contract right offered on Taylor's decision 2 (2026-09-28), text identical to `casualty-landlord-termination-sc` with Alabama named. Ala. Code § 35-9A-406 gives only the tenant rights; nothing in Chapter 9A bars a landlord termination right, and the clause preserves the tenant's statutory rights, so it waives nothing listed in Ala. Code § 35-9A-163(a)(1). Accounting date follows Ala. Code § 35-9A-406(b). Kept separate from `casualty-termination-al` so the statutory tenant rights stay intact. | AL retro 2026-09-30 (SOP 1.8, rule 54t, casualty rows checked first): the clause pointed to \"this Lease's Fire or Casualty Damage terms\", but casualty-termination-al was switched off by the 2026-09-29 scrub (now edu-casualty-termination-al), so AL leases had no such section. Pointers replaced with Alabama law; substance unchanged (Ala. Code § 35-9A-406(a)-(b); Ala. Code § 35-9A-201). Same dangling pointer in casualty-landlord-termination-sc: flagged in AL retro section, not changed. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser from the official Code of Alabama 1975 on ALISON (alison.legislature.state.al.us; whole Code reloaded, 49,638 section versions, control term 0; section text saved and SHA-256 matched to the browser, AL retro sources).",
