    topicKey: "abandoned-property",
    notes: "AL: Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser from the official Code of Alabama 1975 on ALISON (alison.legislature.state.al.us, the Legislature's own code service; Title 35 Chapter 9A read whole, all 48 section numbers, with every history line; newest Chapter 9A amendment Act 2018-473; whole Code loaded, 49,638 section versions including versions effective 2026-10-01 and later; every 2024, 2025 and 2026 act touching landlord-tenant terms screened; AL log §1). Controlling text: Ala. Code § 35-9A-423(c) (re-rent duty at a fair rental, not ahead of other vacant units; new tenancy ends the agreement; periodic tenancies deemed a month or a week); Ala. Code § 35-9A-423(d) ('If a tenant leaves property in the unit more than 14 days after termination pursuant to this chapter, the landlord has no duty to store or protect the tenant's property in the unit and may dispose of it without obligation'); Ala. Code § 35-9A-423(e) (electric service terminated seven consecutive days = abandoned; Act 2014-279); entry on reasonable cause to believe abandonment (Ala. Code § 35-9A-303(b)(5)). History: Act 2006-316; Act 2011-700; Act 2014-279. No notice, storage, inventory or sale procedure and no dollar threshold (contrast `abandoned-property-sc`, $500; `abandoned-property-tn`, 30 days); 'termination pursuant to this chapter' means the 14 days run from a lawful termination, not from a lockout. Landlord liens on household goods unenforceable unless perfected before 2007-01-01; distraint abolished (Ala. Code § 35-9A-425). Manufactured home left on a landlord's lot: separate procedure, Ala. Code Title 35 Chapter 12A (deprioritized, not read beyond titles). | AL retro 2026-09-30 (SOP 1.8, rule 37): added the periodic-tenancy rule. Ala. Code § 35-9A-423(c): \"If the tenancy is from month-to-month or week-to-week, the term of the rental agreement for this purpose is deemed to be a month or a week.\" Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser from the official Code of Alabama 1975 on ALISON (alison.legislature.state.al.us; whole Code reloaded, 49,638 section versions, control term 0; section text saved and SHA-256 matched to the browser, AL retro sources).",
