    notes: "UT: Utah Code Ann. § 57-22-4(7)(a): at or before the start of the rental term, disclose in writing the owner's name, address and telephone number, or those of the person authorized to manage, or, if the manager cannot receive notices, of the person authorized to receive notices and perform the owner's duties. The lease is the practical vehicle (Taylor's PA rule). Utah Code Ann. § 57-22-2(1): a managing agent, leasing agent or resident manager is the owner for notices 'unless the agent or manager specifies otherwise in writing in the rental agreement' (rule 50 choice), carried by the bracketed sentence. Utah Code Ann. § 57-22-4(9): the renter may not sue or withhold performance over a failure. Same statutory shape as agent-capacity-designation-wy; kept as a UT row so no Wyoming row changes (UT log s10). Read section-open 2026-09-29 in the built-in browser from the Legislature's official Utah Code XML on le.utah.gov ('Current Version' files, which print each section's history line; effective dates taken from each section's version id): Title 57 Chapters 17, 20, 21, 22, 24 and 27 and Title 78B Chapter 6 Parts 8 and 8a read whole; Chapter 78B-6a (Laws of Utah 2026, ch. 401) read in the parts cited; the whole Utah Code (96 titles, 28,551 section versions) and the Utah Constitution (23 articles) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits (UT log s1, s17).",
