    notes: "UT: Supersedes returned-payments for UT: its 'not to exceed the maximum amount permitted by applicable law' states only a ceiling (rule 53), and Utah Code Ann. § 57-22-4(5)(b) bars charging a fee not included in the rental agreement or above the amount agreed, so the fee must be a stated figure. Dishonored checks: Utah Code Ann. § 7-15-1(2)(b) ($20 service charge, not collectible if a redeposited check is honored, (3)(b)), (4)-(5) (collection costs up to $35 if the check is not paid within 15 calendar days after a written notice in the Utah Code Ann. § 7-15-2 form is mailed), (7) (civil damages after 30 days). Whether a holder other than a depository institution may contract for more than $20 on a check is unsettled ((8), (9)(b)); the bracket steers the landlord to $20 for checks. Failed electronic payments are contract only. Read section-open 2026-09-29 in the built-in browser from the Legislature's official Utah Code XML on le.utah.gov ('Current Version' files, which print each section's history line; effective dates taken from each section's version id): Title 57 Chapters 17, 20, 21, 22, 24 and 27 and Title 78B Chapter 6 Parts 8 and 8a read whole; Chapter 78B-6a (Laws of Utah 2026, ch. 401) read in the parts cited; the whole Utah Code (96 titles, 28,551 section versions) and the Utah Constitution (23 articles) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits (UT log s1, s17).",
