    notes: "UT: Utah Code Ann. § 57-27-201(1): subject to Utah Code Ann. § 57-1-37, an owner or lessor with actual knowledge that the property is currently contaminated must disclose it 'in a real property lease'; civil action, damages and fees, (3). Once the local health department finds the property decontaminated it is 'stigmatized' (Utah Code Ann. § 57-1-1(8)(c)) and nondisclosure is not a basis for liability (Utah Code Ann. § 57-1-37); edu-stigmatized-property-ut. A property whose contamination is reported in a police action related to manufacturing methamphetamine is also under Title 19, Chapter 6, Part 9 (Utah Code Ann. § 57-27-201(2)(b); Part 9 not read). Read section-open 2026-09-29 in the built-in browser from the Legislature's official Utah Code XML on le.utah.gov ('Current Version' files, which print each section's history line; effective dates taken from each section's version id): Title 57 Chapters 17, 20, 21, 22, 24 and 27 and Title 78B Chapter 6 Parts 8 and 8a read whole; Chapter 78B-6a (Laws of Utah 2026, ch. 401) read in the parts cited; the whole Utah Code (96 titles, 28,551 section versions) and the Utah Constitution (23 articles) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits (UT log s1, s17).",
