    notes: "UT: Opt-in (standing GA decision; rule 54). No casualty rule in the chapters read whole; no separate whole-code 'casualty' search was run. The Utah Fit Premises Act gives the owner a statutory route to end the agreement when the unit is not fit for occupancy after a renter's deficient-condition notice (Utah Code Ann. § 57-22-6(4)(c): written notice by the end of the corrective period; refund of prorated prepaid rent and deposit within 10 calendar days; at least 10 calendar days to vacate) and the renter's rent-abatement remedy ends the agreement (Utah Code Ann. § 57-22-6(4)(a)(i)); the last sentence preserves both. Text follows casualty-termination-pa with Utah references. Read section-open 2026-09-29 in the built-in browser from the Legislature's official Utah Code XML on le.utah.gov ('Current Version' files, which print each section's history line; effective dates taken from each section's version id): Title 57 Chapters 17, 20, 21, 22, 24 and 27 and Title 78B Chapter 6 Parts 8 and 8a read whole; Chapter 78B-6a (Laws of Utah 2026, ch. 401) read in the parts cited; the whole Utah Code (96 titles, 28,551 section versions) and the Utah Constitution (23 articles) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits (UT log s1, s17).",
