    notes: "UT: Opt-in, on Taylor's decision 2026-09-29 (UT log s6). Utah Code Ann. § 78B-6a-405(1) (history line 'Renumbered and Amended by Chapter 401, 2026 General Session', HB 591, effective 2026-05-06; the Utah lease used for source 2 cites the former number as 78B-6-1101(3), not verified): no right of action for a tobacco nuisance if the rental agreement states in writing (a) that smoking is allowed in other units and smoke may drift in and (b) that by signing the renter acknowledges being informed and waives the claim; the clause tracks both elements. 'Tobacco nuisance' is used in Utah Code Ann. §§ 78B-6a-101(10)(b)(x) and -405 but the defined term in Utah Code Ann. § 78B-6a-101(14) is 'Tobacco or illegal substance nuisance' (drift more than once in each of two or more consecutive seven-day periods); drafting mismatch flagged (UT log s10). Companion to smoking-policy (new topic key: companion clause, rule 58). The Utah lease used for source 2 carries this waiver with the pre-2026 citation. Read section-open 2026-09-29 in the built-in browser from the Legislature's official Utah Code XML on le.utah.gov ('Current Version' files, which print each section's history line; effective dates taken from each section's version id): Title 57 Chapters 17, 20, 21, 22, 24 and 27 and Title 78B Chapter 6 Parts 8 and 8a read whole; Chapter 78B-6a (Laws of Utah 2026, ch. 401) read in the parts cited; the whole Utah Code (96 titles, 28,551 section versions) and the Utah Constitution (23 articles) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits (UT log s1, s17).",
