    topicKey: "tenant-rights-statement",
    notes: "IL: 765 ILCS 752/20 (P.A. 103-1031, eff. 1-1-26): a landlord or its agent 'shall attach a copy of the summary of this Act as the first page of any written residential lease they enter into with a tenant, including for a new rental or renewal, and obtain the signature of each tenant in the acknowledgment of receipt at the bottom of each page of the summary'. 765 ILCS 752/15(a)-(b): the Department of Human Rights prepares the summary (Safe Homes Act, the eviction Article, the Human Rights Act, 220 ILCS 5/8-201.6 utility-deposit deferral, 65 ILCS 5/1-2-1.5 and 55 ILCS 5/5-1005.10) with a signature space at the bottom of each page. 765 ILCS 752/25: the signatures are evidence of compliance; without them there is a rebuttable presumption of non-compliance. 765 ILCS 752/30: liability to each tenant for the greater of actual damages up to $2,000 or $100, plus costs and attorney's fees. The current summary seen on the Department's page (dhr.illinois.gov/safer-homes) was version V.2025-12.3, 4 pages, also printed as pages 1-4 of the MainStreet REALTORS 2026 lease (IL log §15); a government publication, not a statute, so the builder must fetch the current version (rule 21 flag). Page-1 conflict with the fee box required on the lease's first page by 765 ILCS 705/35(b): resolved by attaching the summary pages first as an attachment, not part of the lease itself, and opening the lease body with fee-disclosure-first-page-il (Taylor, 2026-09-30; IL log §6.2). The Act defines 'tenant' as a person who entered a written lease (765 ILCS 752/10); an oral lease needs no summary. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
