    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    effectiveFrom: "2026-09-30",
    lastChecked: "2026-09-30",
    topicKey: "fee-transparency",
    notes: "IL: 765 ILCS 705/35(b) (added by P.A. 104-479): 'All non-optional fees, regardless of whether they are one-time fees or recurring fees, shall be explicitly contained on the first page of a lease agreement. If a fee is not explicitly contained on the first page of a lease agreement, a tenant shall not be liable for payment of such fee.' (b)(2): 'In a lease agreement disclosure or unit listing, the landlord must disclose whether utilities are included in rent.' The Act does not define 'non-optional fee'; the box also lists the late fee and returned-payment fee so a court reading them as non-optional finds them on page 1 (a landlord-protective choice, IL log §6.2). (b)(1) listing disclosure is outside the lease (edu-rental-fee-law-il). (c) banned fees: none may be listed (edu-rental-fee-law-il); a 'move-in fee' (as in the MainStreet form) is lawful only if it does not pay for a banned item such as a walk-through or routine maintenance, and renaming does not help (765 ILCS 705/35(c)(9), (c)(11), (e); builder note). Exempt: leases for units in owner-occupied premises of 6 units or fewer (765 ILCS 705/35(e)); the box is harmless there. Effective date: P.A. 104-479 Section 99 says July 1, 2026; the Public Act page, bill status and the ILCS source note say January 1, 2027; applied now on Taylor's decision, 2026-09-30 (IL log §1.2, §6.1). Placement conflict with 765 ILCS 752/20 (summary as first page): IL log §6.2. Chicago and Cook County ordinances may add fee rules (flag, not read). Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
