    lastChecked: "2026-09-30",
    topicKey: "flood-disclosure",
    notes: "IL: 765 ILCS 705/25 (P.A. 103-754, eff. 1-1-25; P.A. 104-417, eff. 8-15-25). (b): every landlord must disclose in writing before signing whether the property is in the FEMA Special Flood Hazard Area and any actual knowledge of flooding of the property or its parking areas and its frequency; 'Such disclosure shall also be included in the written lease or the written renewal lease and shall be signed by both parties.' (c): the same for a lower-level unit (garden, basement or first floor) as to flooding in the last 10 years. (d): the written disclosure 'shall look substantially similar to' the prescribed form, reproduced verbatim here, with its paragraph breaks, except for these changes (rule 59): '(Landlord)' becomes 'Landlord ({{landlord_name}})'; each '[ ] is or [ ] is not' becomes a hand-filled '[is / is not]'; each '[ ] times' becomes '[number] times'; and the dotted '(Tenant Signature) (Date)' and '(Landlord Signature) (Date)' lines become 'Tenant signature and date' and 'Landlord signature and date' blanks. Remedies for non-compliance (tenant termination within 30 days, refund of prepaid rent and fees within 15 days, damages for flooded personal property) are in (e). Exempt: farm leases, concession leases, property owned or managed by the Department of Natural Resources ((e), second subsection so lettered). A statewide REQUIRED row: the form also covers the 'not aware / 0 times' case, so every non-exempt lease carries it. The form is a statutory form and a separate pre-signing writing; the clause cannot replace the pre-signing delivery (rule 48; builder note). Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
