    notes: "IL: 420 ILCS 46/26 (P.A. 103-298, eff. 1-1-24; leases entered on or after that date, (g)). (a): at application, before a lease is entered into, or on request during the term, the lessor provides the IEMA pamphlet, copies of records or reports indicating a radon hazard, and the Disclosure of Information on Radon Hazards to Tenants form in (f). (f): the form, reproduced verbatim except that the dotted blanks become lines, the unit address is filled from {{property_address}}, and a period follows the two headings when run into one field (rule 59). CONDITIONAL: 420 ILCS 46/20(9) excludes 'Transfers of any residential dwelling unit located on the third story or higher above ground level', and 'transfers' includes leases. Tenant rights (90-day test and termination, (b)-(c), (e); no deposit deduction for testing or mitigation, 420 ILCS 46/30(c)) are in edu-radon-tenant-rights-il. P.A. 104-852 (general revisory act, eff. 8-21-2026, not yet compiled) makes only technical changes to 420 ILCS 46/26(b) and leaves the (f) form unchanged (IL log §1.2). 420 ILCS 46/15 still says the Act applies to leased properties 'to the extent specified in Section 25', a repealed section (stale cross-reference, IL log §10; rule 77). Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
