    lastChecked: "2026-09-30",
    topicKey: "security-deposit-return",
    notes: "IL: Supersedes security-deposit-return for IL. 765 ILCS 710/1(a) (P.A. 103-224, eff. 1-1-24): no withholding for property damage unless, within 30 days of the date the lessee vacated or the date the lessee's right of possession ends, whichever is later, the lessor furnishes by personal delivery, postmarked mail to the last known address or email to a verified email address provided by the lessee, an itemized statement with estimated or actual costs and paid receipts; receipts within 30 days after an estimate; otherwise return in full within 45 days of vacating, in person or by postmarked mail. Lessor's own labor may be charged at reasonable cost. No liability if the lessee gives no mailing or email address (the forwarding-address sentence serves the landlord). 765 ILCS 710/1(b): verified statement where receipts cannot be produced through no fault of the lessor. 765 ILCS 710/1(c): refusal or bad faith plus failure to return makes the lessor liable for twice the deposit due, costs and attorney's fees (edu-deposit-return-rules-il). The statute has no unit-count threshold since P.A. 103-224. The 45-day outer limit for a balance after deductions is a lease promise the statute does not state for that case; it matches the statute's full-return deadline (IL log §6). Deposit interest for 25+ unit properties: edu-deposit-interest-il. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
