    topicKey: "abandoned-property",
    notes: "IL: No Illinois statute sets a procedure for a residential tenant's property left behind in a house or apartment: whole-code battery 19 (abandon near landlord/lessee/tenant terms) found only 735 ILCS 5/9-318 (crops on abandoned premises), 765 ILCS 745/9.5 (mobile homes, out of scope) and unrelated hits; batteries 67 and 87 found no deposit rule. The shared surrender-end-of-term-ks-ne clause, tagged IL, points to this Section, so a contract procedure is supplied (as abandoned-property-pa and -ut do on statute). Distress for rent (735 ILCS 5/9-301 to 5/9-321) is a separate court-supervised remedy not used by this Section. Case law on conversion and on when a tenancy is abandoned was not read; the notice period is a landlord choice with a floor of 10 days as a caution, not a statutory figure (IL log §6). Unauthorized occupants: 735 ILCS 5/9-102(e) (edu-unauthorized-occupants-il). Towing: 625 ILCS 5/4-203(f). Chicago's ordinance has its own rules (flag, not read). Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
