    topicKey: "alarm-duties",
    notes: "IL: 425 ILCS 60/3(d) (Smoke Detector Act) and 430 ILCS 135/10(c) (P.A. 94-741, Carbon Monoxide Alarm Detector Act): the owner supplies and installs required detectors and alarms; 'The owner shall be responsible for providing one tenant per dwelling unit with written information regarding detector testing and maintenance' (the Lease is the vehicle, hence REQUIRED); the tenant tests and provides general maintenance for detectors in the unit, notifies the owner in writing of deficiencies it cannot correct, replaces required batteries (the owner ensures batteries work at possession) and gives access to correct reported deficiencies; the owner makes reasonable efforts to test and maintain detectors in common stairwells and hallways (smoke detectors only, 425 ILCS 60/3(d)). Placement and device rules (425 ILCS 60/3(a)-(c), (e)-(f); 430 ILCS 135/10(a)-(b), (d)) are for the landlord, not the lease. Restating the tenant duties serves the landlord. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
