    lastChecked: "2026-09-30",
    topicKey: "rent-concession",
    notes: "IL: 765 ILCS 730/2 (P.A. 88-45): a rent concession is a credit on the rent, a rebate, a rent-free or reduced-rent period, or any other valuable thing given 'without express mention thereof in the lease'. 765 ILCS 730/3: when a concession is made, the lessor must cause the lease to bear the legend 'Concession Granted' across its face in letters at least one-half inch high and a memorandum of each concession; failure is unlawful. 765 ILCS 730/4 and 765 ILCS 730/6: exhibiting such a lease without the legend to a buyer, lessee or lender is unlawful, a Class A misdemeanor when done to sell or borrow. Stating the concession expressly in the lease takes it outside the definition. Repairs and decorating, and waivers of non-rent terms, are not concessions (765 ILCS 730/2). Farm property excluded (765 ILCS 730/5a). New topic_key: no state has a row on this subject (rule 58). Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
