    topicKey: "keys",
    notes: "IL: Supersedes keys for IL. 765 ILCS 705/15(b) (P.A. 97-470): in counties of more than 3,000,000 (Cook County; population derived from secondary knowledge, census not read, IL log §7), after a unit is vacated and on or before the day a new lessee takes possession, the lessor must change or rekey the lock; (c) liability for theft attributable to failure; (d) not applicable where the lessee obtained the right to rekey under a written lease; (e) exempt: owner-occupied buildings of 4 units or fewer, rooms in owner-occupied homes. Charging a departing tenant for the rekey the statute already requires is doubtful and could read as a routine-maintenance fee barred by 765 ILCS 705/35(c)(9) for leases the fee law covers; the added exception removes that exposure statewide (rule 32: one version lawful everywhere in Illinois). Optional tenant rekey right: tenant-rekey-right-il. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
