    notes: "IL: Optional clause (rule 54: a landlord right that exists only if the parties sign the addendum). 765 ILCS 705/5(a) (P.A. 100-173): Class X felony charge during the term plus probable cause or indictment voids the lease at the lessor's option; 5-day posted notice on circuit clerk forms; (b) no deposit forfeiture solely for this eviction; (c) costs rules; (d): 'The provisions of this Section are enforceable only if the lessee or occupant and the owner or owner's assignee have executed a lease addendum for drug free housing as promulgated by the United States Department of Housing and Urban Development or a substantially similar document.' The HUD addendum itself (a federal form) was not read (rule 21 flag); the bracket makes signing it a condition of use. New companion topic_key beside criminal-activity (rule 58). Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
