    topicKey: "casualty-termination",
    notes: "ID: Optional clause (rule 54; standing GA decision: offer landlord casualty termination where no statute controls). CONFIRMED ABSENT: no Idaho statute on destruction of leased premises or casualty termination (whole-code search for destruction, casualty or fire near lease, tenant, lessee or rental agreement: 48 hits in 45 sections, none a residential-tenancy rule). Idaho Code § 6-320(a) still gives the tenant a damages and specific-performance action for waterproofing, facilities and hazards; the clause preserves it. Same text as casualty-termination-pa and casualty-termination-il with Idaho named. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser from legislature.idaho.gov section pages, which print each section's history line and are current through the 2026 session (the site's currency page; its chapter PDFs lag and omit 2026 changes, so every section the 2026 session touched was reloaded from its current page): Idaho Code Title 6, Chapter 3 (all 28 sections in the official chapter index, Idaho Code §§ 6-301 to 6-324; no 6-306, 6-307 or 6-311B is listed) and Title 55, Chapters 2 and 3 read whole; the whole Idaho Code (1,470 chapter PDFs plus 1,166 current 2026-affected sections, 22,935 sections) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits (ID log s1, s17).",
