    topicKey: "security-deposit-use",
    notes: "MO: Overrides security-deposit-use, whose 'remedy a Tenant default under this Lease' is broader than Missouri's closed list: the landlord 'may withhold from the security deposit only such amounts as are reasonably necessary' for (1) a default in rent due under the rental agreement, (2) restoring the dwelling unit to its condition at the commencement of the tenancy, ordinary wear and tear excepted, and (3) actual damages from the tenant's failure to give adequate notice to terminate, with reasonable mitigation (Mo. Rev. Stat. § 535.300(4)). Cap: no more than two months' rent (Mo. Rev. Stat. § 535.300(1)); the builder must keep {{security_deposit}} at or below twice {{monthly_rent}} (MO log §10). The cap is stated in rent, not per lease year, so it does not reset on renewal (rule 37). Holding: in a federally insured bank, credit union or depository institution, interest to the landlord; housing authorities and other government landlords are exempt from the holding rule (Mo. Rev. Stat. § 535.300(2)). No deduction in place of rent and no limit on recovering actual damages beyond the deposit (Mo. Rev. Stat. § 535.300(7)). A pet deposit is not a security deposit (Mo. Rev. Stat. § 535.300(8)); see pet-policy-mo. Local deposit limits are preempted (Mo. Rev. Stat. § 441.043(2)(3)). Carpet cleaning amounts may be agreed only with the statutory notice (deposit-carpet-cleaning-mo). Rule 15: written section-open. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser from revisor.mo.gov (Missouri Revisor of Statutes, which prints each section with its history line and version date and describes its text as unofficial and uncertified): Chapters 441, 534 and 535 read whole (72, 45 and 23 sections as indexed); the whole Revised Statutes of Missouri and the Missouri Constitution (30,836 entries) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits (MO log §1, MO log §17).",
