    notes: "MO: Instruction 24 family. Mo. Rev. Stat. § 535.300(3): within 30 days after the date of termination of the tenancy the landlord shall return the full deposit or furnish a written itemized list of the damages for which any portion is withheld, along with the balance; mailing the statement and payment to the tenant's last known address complies. Mo. Rev. Stat. § 535.300(5): reasonable written notice of the date and time of the move-out inspection, at the last known address or in person; inspection at a reasonable time; tenant's right to be present. Penalty for wrongful withholding: twice the amount wrongfully withheld (Mo. Rev. Stat. § 535.300(6); edu-security-deposit-rules-mo). The 30 days run from the end of the tenancy, not from move-out or the tenant's demand; the statute does not let the lease fix another period (rule 50). The forwarding-address sentence is a tenant step the statute does not impose; it does not extend the deadline. Rule 15: written section-open. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser from revisor.mo.gov (Missouri Revisor of Statutes, which prints each section with its history line and version date and describes its text as unofficial and uncertified): Chapters 441, 534 and 535 read whole (72, 45 and 23 sections as indexed); the whole Revised Statutes of Missouri and the Missouri Constitution (30,836 entries) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits (MO log §1, MO log §17).",
