    topicKey: "returned-payments",
    notes: "MO: Overrides returned-payments, whose 'not to exceed the maximum amount permitted by applicable law' states only a ceiling (rule 53). Mo. Rev. Stat. § 570.120(6)(2): if a dishonored or returned check is not referred to the prosecuting or circuit attorney, the party to whom it was issued, or a holder, 'may collect from the issuer, in addition to the face amount of the check, a reasonable service charge, not to exceed twenty-five dollars, plus an amount equal to the actual charge by the depository institution for the return of each unpaid or dishonored instrument'. The cap is stated for checks; the section's offense provisions also reach 'any other form of presentment involving the transmission of account information', but subdivision (6)(2) speaks only of a 'check'; whether it caps fees on failed electronic payments is not settled by the text. The bracket states the landlord's figure (rule 55); the builder should cap a check fee at $25 plus the bank's actual charge (MO log §10). Section read whole and saved (outside-title, source 4). Rule 15: written section-open. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser from revisor.mo.gov (Missouri Revisor of Statutes, which prints each section with its history line and version date and describes its text as unofficial and uncertified): Chapters 441, 534 and 535 read whole (72, 45 and 23 sections as indexed); the whole Revised Statutes of Missouri and the Missouri Constitution (30,836 entries) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits (MO log §1, MO log §17).",
