    notes: "IN: Optional clause (rule 54; standing GA decision: offer landlord casualty termination where no statute controls it). No Indiana statute addresses fire or casualty damage to leased residential premises, rent abatement or termination (IN battery 121: 41 sections, none a residential casualty rule; known-positive passed; whole read of Ind. Code art. 32-31). The landlord's duties to deliver and keep the premises habitable and to maintain systems cannot be waived (Ind. Code §§ 32-31-8-4, 32-31-8-5), and the clause does not waive them. Common-law rules on casualty are case law, not read. Same structure as casualty-termination-mo without a statutory release sentence (edu-casualty-in). Rule 15: written section-open. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser from iga.in.gov (Indiana General Assembly, 2026 Indiana Code, which prints each section with its history line and any future-dated version): Ind. Code art. 32-31 read whole (chapters 1, 2, 2.9, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 8.5, 9, 10, 11 and 12); the whole 2026 Indiana Code (37 title files, 93,246 sections, checked against the site's title index) and the Indiana Constitution loaded for full-text search, control terms 0 hits (IN log §1, IN log §17).",
