    topicKey: "holdover-rate",
    notes: "AZ: NEW 2026-09-30 (SOP 1.13 retro, rule 54 holdover shape, NE 5; Taylor confirmed the rule-54 approach 2026-09-30). A.R.S. §33-1375(C) sets a measure only for a holdover that is 'willful and not in good faith'; an ordinary holdover leaves the landlord actual damages, so the lease may set a measure for the cases the statute leaves out (§33-1314(A)). Model holdover-rate-ga; variable {{holdover_daily_rate}} reused. Companion holdover-az. Unread risks: Arizona liquidated-damages and penalty case law (a rate far above the daily rent may be struck); whether a court treats a holdover charge as rent for §33-1371(C) waiver purposes. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in Taylor's built-in browser from azleg.gov (official compilation; each section fetched twice, heading number checked); saved to the AZ retro source folder with a SHA-256 match to the browser text (AZ retro log, sources).",
