    topicKey: "owner-identity-disclosure",
    notes: "OK: Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 116(A): 'As a part of any rental agreement the lessor shall prominently and in writing identify what person at what address is entitled to accept service or notice under this act', and the landlord or a person authorized to enter into a rental agreement for him shall disclose in writing at or before commencement the name and address of the manager, the owner, or a person authorized to act for the owner for service and notices; the information must be kept current and binds successors. Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 116(B): a person who fails to comply becomes a landlord and agent for service and for the landlord's obligations. 'Landlord' includes a manager who fails to comply (Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 102(5)); notices to a landlord who cannot be served personally go by certified mail to the Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 116 person (Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 111(E)). Builder: 'prominently' (OK log §4) - heading in capitals and bold, placed with the parties. Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 116 read whole. Rule 15: written section-open. Read section-open 2026-09-30 to 2026-10-01 in the built-in browser from oklegislature.gov (Oklahoma Legislative Service Bureau whole-title files, statutes last updated Nov. 18, 2025, which print each section with its history line; checked against OSCN's history notes where cited): Okla. Stat. tit. 41, §§ 1-201, read whole and Okla. Stat. tit. 12, §§ 1148.1-1148.16, read whole; the whole Oklahoma Statutes (88 title files, 47,809 sections, checked against each file's own index) and the Oklahoma Constitution loaded for full-text search, control terms 0 hits (OK log §1, OK log §17).",
