    topicKey: "pet-policy",
    notes: "OK: Base pet-policy not tagged: its indemnity sentence ('will indemnify Landlord from claims arising from Tenant's pet(s)') is a term Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 113(A)(4) makes unenforceable if it reaches liability arising from the parties' acts or omissions in operating or maintaining the premises (scope case law unread; Kansas, under the same URLTA ban, dropped the sentence, pet-policy-ks), and its entry-and-removal sentence lets the landlord enter beyond Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 128 (consent, one day's notice, or emergency; Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 128(D): no other access during the tenancy except as the act provides or by court order). Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 102(2): 'Deposit' is any money required as security and returnable at termination, so a refundable pet deposit is held in escrow and returned under Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 115 (edu-pet-deposit-ok); a nonrefundable pet fee or pet rent is 'rent' (Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 102(11)). Assistance animals: Okla. Stat. tit. 41, §§ 113.1, 113.2 (assistance-animal-accommodation, edu-assistance-animals-ok). Remedy for a pet breach: Okla. Stat. tit. 41, § 132 (notice and cure). Rule 15: written section-open. Read section-open 2026-09-30 to 2026-10-01 in the built-in browser from oklegislature.gov (Oklahoma Legislative Service Bureau whole-title files, statutes last updated Nov. 18, 2025, which print each section with its history line; checked against OSCN's history notes where cited): Okla. Stat. tit. 41, §§ 1-201, read whole and Okla. Stat. tit. 12, §§ 1148.1-1148.16, read whole; the whole Oklahoma Statutes (88 title files, 47,809 sections, checked against each file's own index) and the Oklahoma Constitution loaded for full-text search, control terms 0 hits (OK log §1, OK log §17).",
