    topicKey: "tenant-repair-agreement",
    notes: "IA: TAYLOR'S DECISION (2026-10-02, IA log §6.2): Option 1, matching Arizona (`maintenance-allocation-az`) and Nebraska; model on `maintenance-allocation-az` and include Iowa Code § 562A.15(4). Controlling text: Iowa Code § 562A.15(2) (single family residence: landlord and tenant may agree in writing that the tenant performs the (1)(a)(5) and (6) duties and specified repairs, maintenance tasks, alterations and remodeling, only if entered into in good faith); Iowa Code § 562A.15(3) (any other dwelling unit: only if in good faith, 'set forth in a separate writing signed by the parties and supported by adequate consideration', and not diminishing or affecting the landlord's obligation to other tenants); Iowa Code § 562A.15(4) ('The landlord shall not treat performance of the separate agreement described in subsection 3 as a condition to an obligation or performance of a rental agreement'); Iowa Code § 562A.15(1)(a)(1)-(2), (b) (code compliance and habitability remain the landlord's); Iowa Code § 562A.6(15) ('single family residence'). Rule 48: separate document. The snow checkbox is limited to areas only Tenant uses (common areas are the landlord's, Iowa Code § 562A.15(1)(a)(3)). Builder property-type gate: gap (IA log §10). Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from legis.iowa.gov (Iowa Code 2026 chapter XML; the whole Code and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, IA log §1); no 2025 or 2026 act amends ch. 562A or ch. 648 (IA log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
