    lastChecked: "2026-10-02",
    topicKey: "termination-notice",
    notes: "IA: Iowa Code § 562A.34(1) (week-to-week: written notice at least ten days before the termination date specified in the notice); Iowa Code § 562A.34(2) (month-to-month: written notice at least thirty days prior to the periodic rental date specified in the notice); Iowa Code § 562A.29A(1) (a landlord's Iowa Code § 562A.34 notice is served by signed acknowledgment, personal service, or posting plus regular and certified mail; mail complete four days after mailing, Iowa Code § 562A.29A(2)); a tenant's notice under Iowa Code § 562A.8(1)(b). Iowa Code § 562A.9(5): without a definite term the tenancy is month-to-month (week-to-week for a roomer paying weekly). The bracketed periods are floors (rule 53). Fixed terms: `edu-end-of-term-ia` (Iowa Code §§ 562.6, 562A.34(3)). Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from legis.iowa.gov (Iowa Code 2026 chapter XML; the whole Code and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, IA log §1); no 2025 or 2026 act amends ch. 562A or ch. 648 (IA log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
